{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age","id":1487660,"title":"How would the Traditions react to the power of Blood Magic in the modern age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-23T16:26:47-07:00","id":1487660,"title":"How would the Traditions react to the power of Blood Magic in the modern age?","content":"One of the big things that are kept constant between the game lines is how little each faction knows about one another. Let's say that for this scenario, the mages have more information on the kindred than usual. This information is about the different types of blood magic that many vampires use. The Order of Hermes probably already has an inkling of what thaumaturgy can do, but that was during a very early period in Tremere history when thaumaturgy itself was still pretty new, now in the modern age, thaumaturgy has advanced to the point that it no doubt makes practitioners of other schools feel threatened. Especially the ones that practice a blood magic tradition older than thaumaturgy itself.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to paste a list of all the types of blood magic used by vampires. None of you probably need it, but it may serve as a refresher on the Blood Magic Traditions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1) 4 different types of Setite Sorcery practiced by 4 different FoS bloodlines, with the most common being Akhu, and another lesser known type known as Nahuallotl which is most likely practiced exclusively by the Tlacique.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2) Koldunic Sorcery practiced by the Kolduns of Old Clan Tzimisce.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3) Assamite Sorcery/Dur-An-Ki practiced by the Assamite Sorcerer Caste, and a few Metheleusas. Becomes an in clan discipline for the Assamites in V5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4) Sadhana practiced by the Indian Venture bloodline known as Danava, Daitya (FoS Bloodline), a few Indian vampires that come from other clans, and the Trimira (Indian Tremere) which accept other vampires from different clans.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5) Different types of necromancy practiced by the Giovanni, Samedi, Nagraja, some Haitian Lassombra, and some Serpents of Light. Replace by Oblivion for the Hecate in V5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6) Abyss Mysticism practiced by the mystics of clan Lassombra.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7) Thaumaturgy and Selinic Thaumaturgy practiced by the Tremere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">8) Dark Thaumaturgy practiced by Baali, Angellis Ater, and practically every infernalist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9) Wanga practiced by a couple Samedi vampires, but used to a greater degree by the Serpents of Light.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10) Anarch Sorcery that includes 4 different &quot;Waves&quot; (Think of them as different schools) practiced by the Anarchs.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">11) Sihr practiced by Islamic kindred.</span><br /> <br /> I can see mages who are burnt-out with fighting the technocracy see turning Blood Magic as a practical option, although it's not as powerful as true magick it's not prone to paradox and blood is far easier to aquire than quintessence. Dreamspeaker are the most likely to be interested in Assamite sorcery, Verbena would probably feel comfortable with Koldunic Sorcery, Cult of Ecstasy would probably find New Age Sorcery (&quot;Wave&quot; of anarch sorcery) appealing, there's Hativist Thaumathurgy for the Virtual Adepts, OoH would, of course, find themselves gravitating towards thaumaturgy, e.t.c.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to include you need to be a vampire, but hey if Tremere thought it was a good option, so would others....<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-23-2022, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T16:56:49-07:00","id":1487661,"title":"","content":"It's not conversible. Blood Magic is not true magik.<br /> <br /> That being said, SOME occult knowledge could be translated from one another; that however cuts both ways.<br /> <br /> The Traditions could become some serious teachers for cainite magicians, and when I say that, I really mean it. Just imagine what kind of blood magic could come from studying Etherites and VAs.<br /> <br /> That of course would be easier said than done. Such a relantionship would be next to impossible, particularly given the many divisions of the cainites. Also, because I dont think the cainites would be all too enthusiastic about the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Localized exchanges however are possible, and I wouldnt find hard to view the Traditions desperate enough to consider such afiliations on more regular bases. So, such exchanges of occult knowledge are possible, and after it goes to small groups, it spreads over. The mages however are more likely to spread knowledge amongst themselves, so the Traditions would probably gain a lot more from this than the vampires, but individual vampires would also benefit.<br /> <br /> Now, given how those powers arent interchangeable, what the Traditions would gain would be knowledge on what the cainites can do, and interesting uses of their spheres.<br /> <br /> For example, &quot;blood bond&quot; aint something that Mages naturally have, but it's an interesting idea; Prime 1 could be used to replicate such a powerful effect. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:26:57-07:00","id":1487663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487661#post1487661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not conversible. Blood Magic is not true magik.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, &quot;blood bond&quot; aint something that Mages naturally have, but it's an interesting idea; Prime 1 could be used to replicate such a powerful effect. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im guessing blood bond would also require some life and mind as well, maybe even spirit since many believe vampirism is a spiritual curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-23-2022, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T20:31:26-07:00","id":1487681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487663#post1487663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im guessing blood bond would also require some life and mind as well, maybe even spirit since many believe vampirism is a spiritual curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You see, this is a problem for Mage, people just throw in Spheres by the &quot;feeling&quot;, rather than looking at each level description exactly. With Prime 1 you can &quot;tune in&quot; the ressonance. Oh, by the way, my bad, it's actually Prime 2, because it's a living being. See? All I have to do is check out the Spheres descriptions. So, with Prime 2 I can &quot;attune&quot; someone's ressonance to my own.<br /> <br /> Now, what happens when we do that?<br /> <br /> Simple, it turns another living being as &quot;part of yourself&quot;.<br /> <br /> Remember the correspondence table?<br /> <br /> Well, in order to affect someone having a &quot;body sample&quot; of the target, you dont need extra successes for correspondence.<br /> <br /> That's what Prime 1 does for material objects, and Prime 2 does for living beings.<br /> <br /> So, using Prime 2, you basically make the person become as if it were &quot;part of your body&quot;. That's how deep this connection can be.<br /> <br /> You dont need life, nor mind, nor spirit, because you're NOT dominating her body, mind or soul.<br /> <br /> You're just making her energies to become so in tune with yours that you'll basicallyl share them.<br /> <br /> Ready the description of Prime. You'll see that the effect is basically that of a Blood Bound","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T20:53:58-07:00","id":1487682,"title":"","content":"The Blood Bond makes someone love and adore the vampire so much that they become insanely loyal, obsessed and subordinate to the point that the blood bonded individual would throw themself in front of a car without a second thought (or indeed without even thinking about it at all) if it meant protecting their dominator.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem like something that Prime 2, on its own, could inflict on someone and definitely seems like it would be involve some level of Mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T21:22:41-07:00","id":1487684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487661#post1487661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not conversible. Blood Magic is not true magik.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, it's not that simple. The Ghoul Merit allows a mage to develop the physical enhancement Disciplines, plus a fourth Discipline from the Clan of the vampire who ghouled the mage. If I recall correctly, the various Kindred sorceries count as Disciplines for this purpose; so if a mage is ghouled by a Tremere, he should be able to pick up some Thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> Likewise, there's an option in the V20 Black Hand book whereby a vampire can blood bond a mage and gain access to her Avatar, allowing the vampire to use True Magick. Granted, what they present is a Foundation-and-Pillars magic; but from what I understand, that was because Foundation-and-Pillars magic can <i>fit</i> in a V20 supplement; the Arete-and-Spheres system can't. However, I see no reason why the principle couldn't be applied to any kind of Awakened Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T21:43:38-07:00","id":1487685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487684#post1487684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, it's not that simple. The Ghoul Merit allows a mage to develop the physical enhancement Disciplines, plus a fourth Discipline from the Clan of the vampire who ghouled the mage. If I recall correctly, the various Kindred sorceries count as Disciplines for this purpose; so if a mage is ghouled by a Tremere, he should be able to pick up some Thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The rules for mage ghouls arent very solid thou. If Im not mistaken, in Blood Treachery I think it was the name? I'd have to check - but anyway, there were rules that Ghouldom literally DESTROYED the Avatar, so not a good trade.<br /> <br /> Also, Disciplines - even blood magic paths - take a long time to master, and pale in comparison to Spheres.<br /> <br /> All in all, not really worth it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487684#post1487684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, there's an option in the V20 Black Hand book whereby a vampire can blood bond a mage and gain access to her Avatar, allowing the vampire to use True Magick. Granted, what they present is a Foundation-and-Pillars magic; but from what I understand, that was because Foundation-and-Pillars magic can <i>fit</i> in a V20 supplement; the Arete-and-Spheres system can't. However, I see no reason why the principle couldn't be applied to any kind of Awakened Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the kind of nonsensical optional rule that would have no room on my tables.<br /> <br /> It would be like having access to the disciplines of a bound blooded vamp. Absolutely ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T21:45:06-07:00","id":1487686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487682#post1487682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blood Bond makes someone love and adore the vampire so much that they become insanely loyal, obsessed and subordinate to the point that the blood bonded individual would throw themself in front of a car without a second thought (or indeed without even thinking about it at all) if it meant protecting their dominator.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem like something that Prime 2, on its own, could inflict on someone and definitely seems like it would be involve some level of Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's simply a matter of successes. If you read Prime description, it's literally what it does. To reach that level of devotion would just probably require many more successes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:57:19-07:00","id":1487698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487685#post1487685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The rules for mage ghouls arent very solid thou. If Im not mistaken, in Blood Treachery I think it was the name? I'd have to check - but anyway, there were rules that Ghouldom literally DESTROYED the Avatar, so not a good trade.<br /> <br /> Also, Disciplines - even blood magic paths - take a long time to master, and pale in comparison to Spheres.<br /> <br /> All in all, not really worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the rules found in M20 Book of Secrets. It definitely presents ghouldom as having its downsides; but mostly that takes the form of Resonance and/or Echoes, not destruction of the Avatar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487685#post1487685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is the kind of nonsensical optional rule that would have no room on my tables.<br /> <br /> It would be like having access to the disciplines of a bound blooded vamp. Absolutely ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still an option for those who want it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T01:50:58-07:00","id":1487702,"title":"","content":"Its functionally very simular to hedge/static magic (which is what It might be) From their perspective its not worth it, at best it's a crude approximation of spheres and can provide some interesting insights at worst its a metaphysical trap for the greedy and shortsighted. Blood treachery explores this issue quite well.<br /> <br /> This is working of v20 dynamic v5 blood magic/oblivion would be considered a complete joke unless they nerf magic in m5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-26-2022, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T03:48:41-07:00","id":1487716,"title":"","content":"I can't see many Mages consider turning to Blood Magic as a viable alternative to True Magick, simply because the difference in power potential is so vast. If I were given the choice between becoming a Mage or turning vampire with Blood Magic, I would pick Mage any time. While high level Blood Magic is undeniably strong, and of any static magic arguably is the strongest, its potential is locked behind Generation. Even then, when you compare it to Archspheres, it pales in level of flexibility.<br /> <br /> Not having to deal with Paradox and becoming immortal are nice deal sweeteners of course, but are they worth killing your Avatar and losing access to dynamic Magick? I would argue no. Forget the Tremere for a moment and look at the other Clans that have dabbled in Blood Magic for far longer. None of them have ever managed to replicate the potential of True Magick despite several thousand years of development, and it wasn't for lack of trying. The Chakravanti who went to Enoch and turned Liches or Nagaraja are probably the best example of that.<br /> <br /> Vitae though is a completely different story. It's arguably the most magickal substance in existence- the insane amount of supernatural properties plus being basically unrefined Tass makes it incredibly attractive to Mages who know about it. In this regard, the different types of Blood Magic are an interesting case study in how to harness its power. Still: for a Mage, any Sorcery is like nibbling crumbs off the plate when they could have the whole cake.<br /> <br /> But! Dynamic Magick didn't stop evolving. Pillars turned into Spheres, which can be altered to fit Paradigm (as for the Conventions) or twisted (in case of the Nephandi). It's not inconceivable that some day a group of Mages decides to take a good hard look at Blood Magic and try to figure out how to employ it without having to deal with the whole Vampire shtick. A dedicated or altered Sphere for Blood Magic would be a terrible idea imo, but it's not outside the realm of possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-24-2022, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T06:53:40-07:00","id":1487727,"title":"","content":"By the way, Mind 2 can also achieve the same result of a Blood Bond, albeit in a more direct way.<br /> <br /> Blood in this case would just be the Focus. Granted, Mages have far better ways of achieving that than vampires do; Blood aint even necessary. Hipnotic stances, drugs, crystals, subliminar messages, &quot;love potions&quot; or &quot;love dust&quot;. And a Mage wouldnt even need 3 nights for that - all it needs is successes.<br /> <br /> Still, it is a good way to particularly enslave vampires. A Mage could &quot;empower&quot; his own Blood using Prime 2, and the happyless vampire that decided to drink from said Mage would find himself &quot;Blood Bonded&quot; to the Mage. And given how blood has a potent effect on vampires, that would have a devastating impact. And granted, a smart Mage could make his own blood become a honey trap, bounding ANY vampires that drink from him in the very first go, with a permanent effect. Vampires would only need to drink once and... Instantly enslaved.<br /> <br /> That would probably come at the expense of some perma paradox, but since it's only 2 points and this is a powerful effect, it is well worthed for smart Mages that deal regularly with vamps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T06:56:01-07:00","id":1487881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age#post1487660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big things that are kept constant between the game lines is how little each faction knows about one another. Let's say that for this scenario, the mages have more information on the kindred than usual. This information is about the different types of blood magic that many vampires use. The Order of Hermes probably already has an inkling of what thaumaturgy can do, but that was during a very early period in Tremere history when thaumaturgy itself was still pretty new, now in the modern age, thaumaturgy has advanced to the point that it no doubt makes practitioners of other schools feel threatened. Especially the ones that practice a blood magic tradition older than thaumaturgy itself.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to include you need to be a vampire, but hey if Tremere thought it was a good option, so would others....<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In your edit is the crux of the problem. The Mages do not want to destroy their souls and their whole philosophical foundations of the cosmos for the paltry rewards that are blood magic. You are pretty much trying to explain to practicing faithful Christians or Muslims that they are silly to follow their God and his Prophets and should follow the Flying Spaghetti Monster instead because it brings better goodies.<br /> <br /> The reason why the whole Tremere thing is seen as horrifying and bad and a reason for multiple wars between OoH and the Tremere is that what they did was trade in temporary limited power for absolute mysteries of the cosmos. That's an insult, heresy and beyond the pale. Sure not every Mage will become an Oracle, but anyone with Arete 3-4 will be vastly more powerful than a linear sorceror that cannot even power its own spells without eating people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T07:30:11-07:00","id":1487883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487881#post1487881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In your edit is the crux of the problem. The Mages do not want to destroy their souls and their whole philosophical foundations of the cosmos for the paltry rewards that are blood magic. You are pretty much trying to explain to practicing faithful Christians or Muslims that they are silly to follow their God and his Prophets and should follow the Flying Spaghetti Monster instead because it brings better goodies.<br /> <br /> The reason why the whole Tremere thing is seen as horrifying and bad and a reason for multiple wars between OoH and the Tremere is that what they did was trade in temporary limited power for absolute mysteries of the cosmos. That's an insult, heresy and beyond the pale. Sure not every Mage will become an Oracle, but anyone with Arete 3-4 will be vastly more powerful than a linear sorceror that cannot even power its own spells without eating people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, what happened to the Tremere was an incident. They didnt know they were going to turn into vampires, that was an unfortunate &quot;side effect&quot; from something they thought would bring them eternal life.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's some indication that Goratrix and Tremere knew what was going to happen or at least had a clue; if that's true, the rest of the house were deceived, and would never accept it otherwise. As to why Tremere and Goratrix would make such a trade to begin with, it's hard to say. Tremere was pretty corrupt to begin with, and had already exchanged enlightment for temporal power long before this ordeal, so maybe he thought &quot;what the hell not&quot;, or maybe he hoped to keep his Avatar somehow in the process.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, the members of the house had never intended to turn into vampires, and over the course of their first century, many who were not part of the initual ritual were forcibly embraced without being asked first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:49:08-07:00","id":1487897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487881#post1487881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Whats the point of being a powerful mage when you are stuck with paradox? Plus, there are paths and rituals that can aid a vampire sorcerer in discovering the secrets of the cosmos. spirit manipulation, Ash path, shulpre path, path of karma(reincarnation), Video Pellis (pagan version of Video Nefas). Theres a level 5 ritual called umbral walk that allows you to travel to any part of the umbra you have knowledge about.<br /> <br /> Blood magic isnt that powerful true, but it still has abbilites similar to that of true magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:00:53-07:00","id":1487900,"title":"","content":"If you would rather wallow in the pit with the mediocre offerings of linear magic, death of self and blood addiction speaks more about your fundamental misunderstanding what Mage is actually about than anything else. The only equivalent in Vampire is the Quest for Golconda, but the rewards are so much greater than redemption and peace - they are power beyond ken and comprehension of Reality beyond anything anyone can dream of.<br /> <br /> You'd end your Ascension and be trapped in a forever nightmare of banality, predation, dehumanisation and eventual loss of self. Even the Nephandi have a better outlook than that, and that's really sad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:18:56-07:00","id":1487905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487900#post1487900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you would rather wallow in the pit with the mediocre offerings of linear magic, death of self and blood addiction speaks more about your fundamental misunderstanding what Mage is actually about than anything else. The only equivalent in Vampire is the Quest for Golconda, but the rewards are so much greater than redemption and peace - they are power beyond ken and comprehension of Reality beyond anything anyone can dream of.<br /> <br /> You'd end your Ascension and be trapped in a forever nightmare of banality, predation, dehumanisation and eventual loss of self. Even the Nephandi have a better outlook than that, and that's really sad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres multiple paths of enlightenment for stuff like that, and we see non sabbat vampires having the time of their unlife. Anarch unchained/unbound goes into how younger vampires dont hold the angst of previous generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:21:23-07:00","id":1487906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487905#post1487905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theres multiple paths of enlightenment for stuff like that, and we see non sabbat vampires having the time of their unlife. Anarch unchained/unbound goes into how younger vampires dont hold the angst of previous generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just... go read Mage. Figure out what it's about and what Seeking and Ascension are like. None of what you're talking about works anywhere close to what being a Mage is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:33:01-07:00","id":1487908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487906#post1487906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just... go read Mage. Figure out what it's about and what Seeking and Ascension are like. None of what you're talking about works anywhere close to what being a Mage is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read that part, and all I understood was that it was a self induced near death experience that allowed a mage to gain a deeper understanding.<br /> <br /> I dont exactly know why you replied with this. Its not like every mage ascends. In fact, from what I've read, very few do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:53:44-07:00","id":1487913,"title":"","content":"Ok, so you don't know what either of those two are.<br /> <br /> Ascension is a road, one filled with revelation, joy and cosmic understanding. Seekings are trancendental moments of <b>knowing</b> in which you explore yourself and what your relationship is to you and to the nature of reality filtered through your own head and views of how reality works. Each of the Seekings you take takes you closer and gives you a greater comprehension of yourself and the universe. It's many things for many people, and many never finish the road, but everyone on it has a deeper relationship with the nature of himself and reality than a corpse will ever have. Each of them is a rush way beyond The Kiss. And as harrowing as some of them may be, and while most will not Ascend, being on that road with what it challenges and ultimately validates <b>You and your own Comprehension of the Cosmos.</b><br /> <br /> And in addition to this you get magic. Free, true magic stemming from your beliefs and who you are. Magic that does what you want it to do, what you need it to do. Magic that changes the world into what you dream. You unlock a vast cosmos of impossibility and it's your oyster. What is a bit of paradox here and there if you can change the world and be better? You can actually teach others, and the more they believe with you, the more powerful you all are and the change becomes the world.<br /> <br /> You want to exchange it for linear, highly specialised magic, slavery to the vampires who give it, slavery to blood, a distaste for life and self that only grows as you turn into a monster or an alien. And even if this was good enough, you are trying to sell it to people who are defined by being highly stubborn True Believers who <b>Know</b> their view of reality and Path are the True Way.<br /> <br /> So even if True Magic wasn't vastly more powerful than Blood Magic, there is so much more on that path than just base power. Heck, anyone focused on base power will always end up plateauing on the road to Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:21:55-07:00","id":1487921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487913#post1487913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so you don't know what either of those two are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone knows what the game is about. <br /> <br /> True magick requires qunitessance, which is a lot harder to get than blood. Its prone to paradox, blood magic isnt. There magick isnt subject to consensus, it works the same no matter what you believe in. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:26:49-07:00","id":1487922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487921#post1487921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone knows what the game is about.<br /> <br /> True magick requires qunitessance, which is a lot harder to get than blood. Its prone to paradox, blood magic isnt. There magick isnt subject to consensus, it works the same no matter what you believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. I guess you don't, then. That's a quite fundamental misunderstanding of how quintessence works and a pretty shoddy understanding how of practically everything around you is quintessence and you just need to reach out for it. Plus you only need quintessence if you want to have an easier life at it or craft magical items. Most other things work with enough effort or the right corollary spheres all on their own.True Magick isn't subject to consensus it's subject to your own philosophy. It <i>can</i> cause consequences like Paradox.<br /> <br /> Is there a specific reason you're engaging in this discussion on a Mage forum since you are clearly not into Mage and have already decided you know better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:57:30-07:00","id":1487926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487922#post1487922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well. I guess you don't, then. That's a quite fundamental misunderstanding of how quintessence works and a pretty shoddy understanding how of practically everything around you is quintessence and you just need to reach out for it. Plus you only need quintessence if you want to have an easier life at it or craft magical items. Most other things work with enough effort or the right corollary spheres all on their own.True Magick isn't subject to consensus it's subject to your own philosophy. It <i>can</i> cause consequences like Paradox.<br /> <br /> Is there a specific reason you're engaging in this discussion on a Mage forum since you are clearly not into Mage and have already decided you know better?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then why is consensus a big deal? If that has no true bearing on powers you use, why is it such a big deal? Why is that whenever I read a mage book consesus seems to be held up to some high standard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T13:13:24-07:00","id":1487931,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487926#post1487926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is consensus a big deal? If that has no true bearing on powers you use, why is it such a big deal? Why is that whenever I read a mage book consesus seems to be held up to some high standard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because the Consensus likes to slap mages for using Magick that goes directly against it (it does so causing Paradox). I think what <i>Asmodai </i>it's explaining it's that magick works the other way arround: It's precisely because mages <i>can </i>act against the Consensus, that they can suffer consequences for doing so...<br /> <br /> I think you may be overestimating how big of deal it's Paradox, and, more importantly <i>why and when </i>it's a big deal. Saying &quot;what good it's to have Magick if there's Paradox&quot;, it's a bit like thinking that on average Vampires are incappable of killing, because average vampires follow Humanity...<br /> <br /> I imagine you DON'T think the average vampire it's <i>incappable </i>of killing :P .... BUT it's not <i>as simple</i> as saying Humanity and the Beast aren't big deals. Of course they are. And Vampires on that Path definitely *<i>may* </i>have a problem with killing, and suffer a consequence if the do so too liberaly, but that depends on a lot of factors.<br /> <br /> The Consensus, Paradox, Quintessence. They are all big deals. But each for their own reasons. If you were versed on the reasons, then you would see why it may be hard to imagine a situation where Blood Magick would be so tempting as to kill one's Avatar for it. <hr /><br /> As an example, vampire's <b>immortality it's tempting</b> (maybe not so much as to consider loosing your True Magick and path to Ascencion, but still I think it can be said to be tempting). Why?, well, it's because <i>immortality </i>as an Effect causes<i> Permanent Paradox that accrues over time</i>, making it an uphill battle to keep your imortality going on on Earth. That's why many powerful mages go off-world, there they build their own Realms where and Paradox it's not a problem.<br /> <br /> Casting a fireball, on the other hand...if you have an &quot;object&quot; or something that looks like it could cause a fireball, then it's Coincident and wouldn't cause Paradox. If your Focus or something makes it necesarily Vulgar for some reason, chance it's that it's still a very small deal. On a success it's just onetemporary dot of 'dox ... it's not &quot;good&quot;, but it's not realy bad unless you were already running high on 'dox. And there are ways to deal with that paradox if you don't have time to bleed it out naturally, like feeding it to a Familiar.<br /> <br /> I think Blood Magick could be situationally better, but it doesn't offer that many advantages. So much so that, even if I hadn't to have my mage becoming a vampire, I struggle to see myself expending the <i>experience </i>to have it, knowing that's xp that could have gone to learn a Sphere (surely there are some exploits to be made, but none comes to mind rigth now) .<br /> <br /> Certainly *not tempting* when compared with the disadvantages of becoming a vampire and losing your Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-25-2022, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T14:36:14-07:00","id":1487938,"title":"","content":"Can I eventually get/craft/buy a Private World/Horizon Realm to rule over? No? Then no thanks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Private World<br /> Prerequisites: Resources 7+, Sanctum 5<br /> Owning a city, state, or cloud is cool, but it\u2019s nothing<br /> compared to having your own world, which is what the richest<br /> of the rich do. Why use magic or hypertechnology to bend<br /> the rules of the world when you can completely rewrite them?<br /> Custom-built wonderlands, Private Worlds exist in their own<br /> pocket dimension \u2014 a Horizon Realm. Like many Horizon<br /> Realms, each Private World is connected to portable anchor<br /> point: a Key.<br /> Because of the vast number of incredibly dangerous Realms<br /> within the Horizon, finding a specific Private World without<br /> the Key is virtually impossible and wildly hazardous. Entering<br /> a Private World with the Key is just as hazardous, at least<br /> without an official invitation from the owner. Unauthorized<br /> visitors are rapidly deconstructed, as the Private World recycles<br /> the constituent parts.<br /> System: Private Worlds are an upgrade to Sanctums and<br /> Laboratories (Mage 20, pg. 323-4), providing most of the same<br /> benefits of a \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Sanctum, with the following exceptions:<br /> \u2022 Significantly more room; Sanctums top out at the size<br /> of a small apartment, while Private Worlds are about<br /> the size of the Moon.<br /> \u2022 Private Worlds can be accessed by anyone who touches<br /> the Key and wills themselves into it. By the same token,<br /> no one, not even the owner, can enter the dimension<br /> without the Key, making Keys one of, if not the, most<br /> precious things the owner has.<br /> \u2022 Private Worlds exist in the Horizon, not the Earthly<br /> plane, meaning that absolutely nothing within its<br /> boundaries is subject to the Paradox Effect. Although<br /> this means that rival mages can theoretically invade and<br /> use Effects without suffering Paradox, they\u2019d be fools<br /> to do so because\u2026<br /> \u2022 Uninvited guests suffer one automatic health level in<br /> aggravated damage per turn simply for existing in the<br /> wrong place, as the Private World attempts to deconstruct<br /> them. Inviting someone in is a simple action that the<br /> owner or any invited guest can perform, but only from<br /> within the World. This stipulation has led to more than<br /> a few unintentional deaths.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487921#post1487921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone knows what the game is about.<br /> <br /> True magick requires qunitessance, which is a lot harder to get than blood. Its prone to paradox, blood magic isnt. There magick isnt subject to consensus, it works the same no matter what you believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have quite the wrong impression of Mage casting. You have ZERO need for Quintessence to cast. It's not a Discipline, Mummy Hekau, Fae Art, Werewolf Gift or Wraith Arcanoi. It has no cost since you are bending reality to your own will according to your Paradigm and Beliefs. Quintessence is only useful if you want to reduce the difficulty of casting or want to enchant something permanently/craft an Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T15:01:26-07:00","id":1487946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487926#post1487926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is consensus a big deal? If that has no true bearing on powers you use, why is it such a big deal? Why is that whenever I read a mage book consesus seems to be held up to some high standard?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So let me put it like this. To do what you are passionate about and to experience all life has to offer you need money. Society forces you to contribute to society by being a productive member and generating value from your work, thus generating money and allowing you to experience what life has to offer at the cost of your time (and nerves, and health and...). What would life be like for you if you had infinite money, or if you didn't need money at all to fully experience everything it offers?<br /> <br /> This is the relationship between a True Mage and the Consensus. You can do all sorts of crazy stuff, but wouldn't it be even better if you didn't have to work extra hard or rob a bank to fuel your passions? That's where the Ascension as a communal goal of Humanity comes rather than just the individual path of the Magus. For the average Mage Consensus isn't even that big of a deal as their magic is quite easy when they are in their own places or in places where they are surrounded by their own people. But eventually they want more. They want to go out into the world and change it. And to do more they need other people that believe what they do or even better, other people that can do what they can do! This is what Mage is all about - overcoming boundaries and becoming so much more than the small minded unimaginative petty masses are right now.<br /> <br /> Consensus is a combination of two forces - cosmic constants and collective belief. You can avoid cosmic constants by changing where you are dimensionally or by tapping into enough belief that you bend the constants to your own preferences. This is done by creating Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> So what is Paradox? Paradox is reality hitting back when you push too hard. It can be anything from strange happenings around you, voices following you around, colors twisting a bit, your thumb growing like a root, becoming so mad you redefine reality to be your madness or being hijacked into a different reality to learn a moral story about being more polite to reality. All of these can be minor temporary effects or permanent ones, and it entirely depends on how much total Paradox you have accumulated. The more you have on you, the worse the effect. You can actually have certain amounts of Paradox &quot;clinging&quot; to you and slowly dissapating or being removed through the help of familiars, nodes or even certain costly rituals.<br /> <br /> How do you get Paradox? Now, If you do magic that's sort of kinda of acceptable, you get hit by no paradox. If you do magic that's weird you get hit by small amounts of paradox. You try to rewrite the cosmic constants in our own reality you get a ton of Paradox. None of these cases mean that it explodes in your face immediately or that its necessarily even negative! And you only really gain significant amounts when you do weird stuff over and over again in a short period of time. You take a break, find ways to get rid of Paradox and use slightly more conservative magic outside of your own places and you're fine.<br /> <br /> Going back to my original metaphor Paradox is the cops going after you for robbing banks to fund your crazy lifestyle. Lay low for a while, change your appearance, or even do the time and get out and do more crimes!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T15:35:28-07:00","id":1487947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487946#post1487946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So let me put it like this. To do what you are passionate about and to experience all life has to offer you need money. Society forces you to contribute to society by being a productive member and generating value from your work, thus generating money and allowing you to experience what life has to offer at the cost of your time (and nerves, and health and...). What would life be like for you if you had infinite money, or if you didn't need money at all to fully experience everything it offers?<br /> <br /> This is the relationship between a True Mage and the Consensus. You can do all sorts of crazy stuff, but wouldn't it be even better if you didn't have to work extra hard or rob a bank to fuel your passions? That's where the Ascension as a communal goal of Humanity comes rather than just the individual path of the Magus. For the average Mage Consensus isn't even that big of a deal as their magic is quite easy when they are in their own places or in places where they are surrounded by their own people. But eventually they want more. They want to go out into the world and change it. And to do more they need other people that believe what they do or even better, other people that can do what they can do! This is what Mage is all about - overcoming boundaries and becoming so much more than the small minded unimaginative petty masses are right now.<br /> <br /> Consensus is a combination of two forces - cosmic constants and collective belief. You can avoid cosmic constants by changing where you are dimensionally or by tapping into enough belief that you bend the constants to your own preferences. This is done by creating Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> So what is Paradox? Paradox is reality hitting back when you push too hard. It can be anything from strange happenings around you, voices following you around, colors twisting a bit, your thumb growing like a root, becoming so mad you redefine reality to be your madness or being hijacked into a different reality to learn a moral story about being more polite to reality. All of these can be minor temporary effects or permanent ones, and it entirely depends on how much total Paradox you have accumulated. The more you have on you, the worse the effect. You can actually have certain amounts of Paradox &quot;clinging&quot; to you and slowly dissapating or being removed through the help of familiars, nodes or even certain costly rituals.<br /> <br /> How do you get Paradox? Now, If you do magic that's sort of kinda of acceptable, you get hit by no paradox. If you do magic that's weird you get hit by small amounts of paradox. You try to rewrite the cosmic constants in our own reality you get a ton of Paradox. None of these cases mean that it explodes in your face immediately or that its necessarily even negative! And you only really gain significant amounts when you do weird stuff over and over again in a short period of time. You take a break, find ways to get rid of Paradox and use slightly more conservative magic outside of your own places and you're fine.<br /> <br /> Going back to my original metaphor Paradox is the cops going after you for robbing banks to fund your crazy lifestyle. Lay low for a while, change your appearance, or even do the time and get out and do more crimes!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! This makes sense now! I always had a hard time undestanding what the books were trying to get at, either I'm terrible at reading or your'e good at explaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T05:57:23-07:00","id":1488009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1487947#post1487947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you! This makes sense now! I always had a hard time undestanding what the books were trying to get at, either I'm terrible at reading or your'e good at explaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, Glad it helped. I was pretty sure you were mostly trolling about Vampire supremacy rather than actually interested in what was going on, but I'm really glad the effort was interesting and of use to you. Sorry if it ended up harsher than necessary.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind, which version of Mage did you try reading? M20 is a lovely book, but it's really not friendly to a new reader. Try going through 2E or Revised (just remember that Revised tends to say PARADOX HORRIBLE WE ALL DEAD a lot, and then gives you about 12 ways to ignore it on a deeper reading) if you want to get a solid primer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T06:19:27-07:00","id":1488012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488009#post1488009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, Glad it helped. I was pretty sure you were mostly trolling about Vampire supremacy rather than actually interested in what was going on, but I'm really glad the effort was interesting and of use to you. Sorry if it ended up harsher than necessary.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind, which version of Mage did you try reading? M20 is a lovely book, but it's really not friendly to a new reader. Try going through 2E or Revised (just remember that Revised tends to say PARADOX HORRIBLE WE ALL DEAD a lot, and then gives you about 12 ways to ignore it on a deeper reading) if you want to get a solid primer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Intro to the traditions, and most of the technocratic and tradition books, I also read path of screams. They may have been revised","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T06:27:39-07:00","id":1488013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488012#post1488012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Intro to the traditions, and most of the technocratic and tradition books, I also read path of screams. They may have been revised</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the supplements (sounds like Revised with a smatter of 2E), but which core I meant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T06:30:34-07:00","id":1488014,"title":"","content":"Do you mean \u201cGuide to the Traditions\u201d? That was a Revised book. As for the Tradition Books: if they had metallic covers, they were first or second edition; if not, they also were Revised. <br /> <br /> Path of Screams definitely was <i>not</i> Revised; it was Sorcerers Crusade. That said, it was written from the perspective of the Fallen not being something you should want to play. It's been a while since I've read it; but I seem to recall that part of the \u201cyou shouldn't want to play this\u201d attitude took the form of leaning heavily into what the downsides of being Fallen are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T06:43:10-07:00","id":1488015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488013#post1488013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the supplements (sounds like Revised with a smatter of 2E), but which core I meant?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bYeah I think thats what it was. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:44:34-07:00","id":1488025,"title":"","content":"So you've gone deep into splatbooks and an antagonist book and never really read the core, then? May I suggest you get 2E/Revised and just read the part on what magic is, what paradigm is, what consensus and paradox are? You've gotten a lot of fluff awareness but not the basic philosophy behind Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T10:33:05-07:00","id":1488049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488025#post1488025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you've gone deep into splatbooks and an antagonist book and never really read the core, then? May I suggest you get 2E/Revised and just read the part on what magic is, what paradigm is, what consensus and paradox are? You've gotten a lot of fluff awareness but not the basic philosophy behind Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I'll do that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:01:00-07:00","id":1488055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488049#post1488049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I'll do that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is a bit weird because it's more a philosphical exercise about Dharma. the nature of reality, ethics of godhood and a weird take on self actualisation through a game. For a lot of people that's a problematic thing to digest even without the fact that the corebooks can be weird and obtuse about it. Good luck!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:30:07-07:00","id":1488060,"title":"","content":"It also doesn't help that the philosophy of Mage has evolved and become more sophisticated over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:41:05-07:00","id":1488065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487660-how-would-the-traditions-react-to-the-power-of-blood-magic-in-the-modern-age?p=1488060#post1488060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't help that the philosophy of Mage has evolved and become more sophisticated over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It's why I honestly dread M5 in Paradoxes hands. It takes a lot of effort to explain it and get it straight and they don't really seem like the people that would care.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:55:48-07:00","id":1488068,"title":"","content":"That's *not* going to be an easy job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T16:47:34-07:00","id":1488110,"title":"","content":"To be blunt, I do not have particularly high expectations for m5. To the point its generating low key anxiety they're going to either fuck up or remove my favourite factions. (Ooh and verbenna). I suspect we'll loose a lot in translation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-26-2022, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theon